let auditPrompt = `First step only: audit the attached wireframe against this file's existing Design System. Do not create or edit any Figma layers yet.

Use “Turn 26 Plates Pane.html” as the content and behavior source of truth for the future high-fidelity mockups. Use frames 26a–26f and 26h. Ignore frame 26g completely, including its collapsed controls and rail. Do not revisit or redesign collapse behavior.

Inspect the current Design System page and identify:
1. reusable components, variants, variables, text styles, icons, and patterns that already cover the wireframe;
2. standard reusable components that are missing and should be added before mockup work;
3. the smallest sensible first component-building step.

The eventual mockups must follow the existing JusPrin visual language and should not introduce one-off primitives where a reusable component belongs. Keep your response concise and specific, grouped as Existing, Missing, and Recommended first step. Stop after the audit and wait for the next instruction.`; await figma.setValue(318, auditPrompt); await figma.click(321); await figma.getAXState();

let rowPrompt = `Build only the first recommended design-system foundation: the reusable hierarchical Plate/Object Row component set on the Design System page. Do not create any high-fidelity mockup frames yet, and do not build the tabs, Project patterns, or anything related to 26g.

Use the existing JusPrin semantic color variables, spacing/radius variables, text styles, Icon, Button/Icon, and Swatch components. Match the established Tool Panel visual language.

The component set must support the wireframe states needed later without one-off primitives:
- row kind: plate and object;
- plate: active/expanded or folded, plate name, Sliced/Needs slice, optional computed summary, optional lock, optional customization mark, optional overflow;
- object: name, optional copy count, optional expand control, optional numbered filament swatch, optional “won’t print” text, optional customization mark, optional mesh-error treatment, optional overflow;
- state: default, hover, and selected;
- preserve compact hierarchy and clear alignment at the pane width.

Use sensible component properties and nested instances rather than creating every possible combination as a separate variant. Include a small specimen group showing the important states. Name layers and properties clearly. Stop after this component set is built and summarize exactly what you created.`; await figma.setValue(318, rowPrompt); await figma.click(321); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(229); let tabsPrompt = `Next step only: create the reusable two-tab Plates/Project navigation component on the Design System page. Do not create any mockup frames or Project content patterns yet.

Requirements:
- exactly two tabs: Plates and Project;
- active tab property with Plates and Project values;
- compact sizing aligned to the 334 px Plates pane row width;
- use existing semantic variables, spacing/radius variables, text styles, and icon components where appropriate;
- follow the established JusPrin Tool Panel visual language;
- include clear active, inactive, hover, and keyboard-focus treatments using component properties or variants;
- do not include any collapse button, collapse rail, third segment, or anything from frame 26g;
- add a small specimen showing both active-tab states.

Name the component and properties clearly. Stop after this component is built and summarize what you created.`; await figma.setValue(233, tabsPrompt); await figma.click(236); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(350); let metadataPrompt = `Next step only: create a reusable Project Metadata Preview component on the Design System page. Do not create mockup frames, empty states, print-history records, or anything from 26g.

This compact 334 px component will be used in the Project tab when a 3MF contains model metadata. It must support:
- optional cover thumbnail;
- optional model title;
- optional author/designer;
- optional license shown with the author when present;
- sensible wrapping and truncation for long content;
- no reserved blank space when an optional field is absent;
- default, hover, and keyboard-focus states if the preview is clickable.

Use existing semantic variables, spacing/radius variables, text styles, Icon and image/thumbnail patterns. Follow the Tool Panel visual language. Use component properties for each optional field and editable text properties. Include a small specimen group showing: full metadata, title and author without cover, and title only. Stop after this component is built and summarize exactly what you created.`; await figma.setValue(354, metadataPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(837); let emptyPrompt = `Next step only: create a reusable Project Metadata Empty State component on the Design System page. Do not create mockup frames, print-history patterns, or anything from 26g.

At the 334 px pane width, the component must show an honest, restrained empty state for a 3MF with no model metadata:
- primary copy: “This 3MF has no model information.”;
- optional Edit Project Info action;
- no placeholder fields, invented title, thumbnail shell, or reserved metadata space;
- default, action-hover, and keyboard-focus specimens;
- support an optional short secondary sentence for use in the Details view without becoming a large empty-state card.

Use existing semantic variables, spacing/radius variables, text styles, Icon/Button primitives, and the Tool Panel visual language. Use properties for action visibility and editable text. Add a compact specimen group. Stop after this component is built and summarize exactly what you created.`; await figma.setValue(354, emptyPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(1035); let historyPrompt = `Next step only: create a reusable Project Print History Record component on the Design System page. Do not create mockup frames or anything from 26g.

At the 334 px pane width, support two record types:
1. Detailed record: date, plate, recorded result/status, printer, recorded elapsed time, and an optional separate line labeled “Slice estimate” for material and cost estimates.
2. Count-only record: older history with only a count, such as “1 earlier print,” and a clear “count only” note.

Requirements:
- recorded print facts must be visually distinct from slice estimates;
- never present an estimate as a recorded fact;
- editable text properties for the displayed values;
- optional estimate line with no reserved space when absent;
- sensible Finished and Stopped status treatments using existing semantic variables;
- default, hover, and keyboard-focus states if the record is clickable;
- compact density consistent with existing Pane Action Row and Tool Panel patterns.

Use existing semantic variables, spacing/radius variables, text styles, and Icon components. Add a specimen group with Finished + estimate, Stopped + estimate, detailed without estimate, and count-only. Stop after this component is built and summarize exactly what you created.`; await figma.setValue(354, historyPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(1268); let frame26aPrompt = `Create the first high-fidelity mockup only: frame 26a, “Ordinary two-plate job · Plates tab.” Stop after this single frame is complete.

Create a new page named “Plates & Project Pane” if it does not already exist. On that page, duplicate the most appropriate approved light workspace frame from Main Page as the visual shell. Preserve its top bar, 3D viewport styling, right-side setup panel, toolbars, tokens, and overall JusPrin visual language. Do not modify the source frame.

Replace only the left pane with a high-fidelity implementation of wireframe frame 26a from the attached HTML. Use instances of the new Design System components, especially Tool Panel, Plates/Project Navigation, Plate/Object Row, Button/Icon, Icon, and existing text/spacing/color variables. Do not redraw those components as one-off primitives.

Required 26a content:
- exactly two tabs, Plates active and Project inactive;
- no collapse button, rail, or anything from 26g;
- Plate 1 is active and expanded, labeled “Plate 1,” status “Sliced”;
- object row “Bracket” with ×2 and an expand control; show it as the selected object and keep selection visually synchronized with the two bracket copies in the 3D view;
- Plate 2 is folded, labeled “Plate 2,” status “Needs slice,” computed summary “Knob”;
- a quiet but discoverable “Add plate” action beneath the plate list;
- discreet overflow actions only where the selected/hovered row calls for them;
- top job action should read “Print plate 1”;
- keep the pane present and appropriately proportioned.

Do not add menus, Project content, complex-object states, annotations inside the product UI, or additional mockup frames. Name the new frame “26a · Ordinary two-plate job · Plates”. When finished, select the frame and summarize what you reused and changed.`; await figma.setValue(354, frame26aPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

await figma.click(1487); let cleanupPrompt = `Correction step only: remove the over-componentization I introduced. Preserve the completed frame “26a · Ordinary two-plate job · Plates” visually and structurally as an editable mockup, but clean the Design System back to its prior reusable scope.

First, in frame 26a, detach any instances of the feature-specific components created during this chat while preserving their exact appearance, auto-layout, text, spacing, and layer organization. Rename the resulting ordinary frames/groups clearly so the mockup remains easy to edit.

Then delete these newly created component definitions and their specimen frames from the Design System page:
- Plate/Object Row and Plate/Object Row Specimens;
- Plates/Project Navigation and Navigation Specimens;
- Pane Header;
- Pane Section Label;
- Pane Action Row;
- Project Pane Navigation Specimens;
- Project Metadata Preview and Metadata Preview Specimens;
- Project Metadata Empty State and Empty-State Specimens;
- Project Print History Record and Print History Record Specimens.

Do not delete, rename, move, or modify any component, style, variable, frame, or specimen that existed before this chat. In particular, preserve the existing Tool Panel, Icon, Button/Icon, Swatch, Menu, typography, color, spacing, radius, and elevation assets. Do not create replacement components or new specimens.

When finished, select frame 26a and report exactly which new definitions/specimens were removed and which instances were detached. Stop after cleanup.`; await figma.setValue(354, cleanupPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

let frame26bPrompt = `Create the next high-fidelity mockup only by duplicating the selected frame “26a · Ordinary two-plate job · Plates” on the same “Plates & Project Pane” page. Name the duplicate “26b · Complex plate · Plates”. Stop after this single frame is complete.

Do not create any components, component sets, variants, specimens, styles, or variables. Build the feature-specific pane content as clearly named ordinary auto-layout frames/groups. Reuse only the Design System assets that existed before this project, such as Tool Panel, Icon, Button/Icon, Swatch, Menu primitives, typography, and semantic variables. Keep the source 26a frame unchanged.

Update only the left pane and the viewport content needed to represent wireframe 26b from the attached HTML:
- Plates active, Project inactive; no collapse control or anything from 26g;
- Plate 1 active and expanded, status “Needs slice”;
- expanded object “Case” with filament slot 1 and the compact customization indicator;
- visible children only because they exist: “Case” part with slot 1, “Logo part” with slot 2, “Dense infill” labeled modifier, and “Cable hole” labeled negative part;
- folded object “Bracket” ×4 with slot 3 and “1 won’t print”; its disabled copy should be visually clear in the viewport;
- “Hinge pin” with slot 3 and a visually distinct mesh-error treatment;
- Plate 2 folded, status “Needs slice,” computed summary “3 objects”;
- quiet “Add plate” action;
- “Not on a plate” group shown because it contains “Spacer”;
- top job action reads “Slice plate 1”;
- keep the viewport selection and pane selection synchronized for the Case object and show multiple filament colors in the scene.

Keep the design calm and scannable despite the complexity. Do not add a menu, Project content, annotations inside the product UI, or any additional frame. When finished, select 26b and summarize the changes.`; await figma.setValue(354, frame26bPrompt); await figma.click(357); await figma.getAXState();

